Let's design a self-improve skill.

When claude works, it often makes observations about workarounds it had
to do, that could be incorporated into procedures (scripts, skills,
agents, workflow, etc).

/self-improve should review the claude logs for any of these conditions,
and look for opportunities to add / update / refactor / delete
components in this repo.

The point is that this repo and the toolset used to work with it should
continue to improve over time, and claude should be looking for ways to
do this.

If we do eventually make a skill from this (which I think is likely)
then it should be invokable by the user only.

Sketch a brief spec of what this could look like. Additionally, research
to see what existing skills or techniques exist already, that we can use
off-the-shelf, or learn from and incorporate into a custom component.
